# Test: a reload that would turn the SPD catch-all DISCARD on by default is refused
# Initial config: vpn ipsec with `unmatched bypass`, so the catch-all passes.
# After SIGHUP:   the same block with the `unmatched` leaf removed, so the
#                 YANG default, discard (RFC 4301 Section 4.4.1), would apply.
# Expected: the ike plugin's verify refuses the reload with the message that names
#           the leaf, what stays open, and the two commands that settle it; the
#           reload is not reported complete.
#
# VALIDATES: refuseImplicitDiscard (internal/component/ike/engine/unmatched.go)
#            reached through the real reload pipeline: config file, SIGHUP, the
#            ike plugin's OnConfigVerify.
# PREVENTS: an operator removing `unmatched bypass`, or configuring `vpn ipsec`
#           for the first time, and cutting the router's own control plane
#           (BGP, SSH, DNS) with a default nobody wrote.
#
# The noop dataplane holds the catch-all without CAP_NET_ADMIN
# (internal/component/ike/dataplane/noop.go), so the test runs unprivileged.

option=env:var=ze_test_ike_dataplane:value=noop
option=env:var=ze_test_ike_port:value=$PORT2
option=timeout:value=30s

stdin=ze-bgp:terminator=EOF_CONF
vpn {
	ipsec {
		cookie-threshold 5
		unmatched bypass
	}
}
EOF_CONF

tmpfs=config2.conf:terminator=EOF_CONF2
vpn {
	ipsec {
		cookie-threshold 5
	}
}
EOF_CONF2

cmd=background:seq=1:exec=le test fixture reload/tx-protocol-sighup-trigger
cmd=foreground:seq=2:exec=ze -:stdin=ze-bgp:timeout=25s

await=stderr:contains=reload error:then=stop
expect=stderr:contains=this commit turns on the SPD catch-all DISCARD without saying so
expect=stderr:contains=`vpn ipsec unmatched` is not set and its default is discard (RFC 4301 Section 4.4.1)
expect=stderr:contains=the 0 `vpn ipsec policy` bypass entries stay open
expect=stderr:contains=`set vpn ipsec unmatched bypass` to keep passing that traffic
reject=stderr:contains=sighup reload complete
reject=stderr:pattern=panic
